      children: "Design systems are often pitched as a way to “move faster,” but the honest value is that they reduce decision fatigue and repeated arguments. A system gives you reusable components, tokens, and patterns that encode prior decisions. That's not glamour-it's governance. The catch is that a design system only works when it's treated like a product with owners, versioning, and a backlog. If it's treated like a one-time “library project,” it becomes stale, teams fork components, and the system quietly dies. The best teams accept that a system is never finished, because the product isn't finished."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
